+# Supplier Invoice Create presentation
+
+FRO-347's approved comfortable Create-page presentation is prepared here as
+controlled React components. It is **unconnected preparation**, not a working
+Supplier Invoice feature or completion of the ticket's acceptance criteria.
+There is no route, menu entry, service, authority, persistence or backend change.
+
+## Components and state ownership
+
+- `components/supplier-invoice-create-layout.tsx` composes the existing
+  `TopBar`, `Card` and `Tabs` primitives. It renders the heading, Overview /
+  Documents, staged count, relationship fields, invoice fields, read-only VAT
+  section and supplied actions. Keyboard tab activation and roving focus are
+  completed locally. Comfortable density is scoped to the layout, with four,
+  two and one columns at the approved breakpoints.
+- `components/supplier-invoice-document-queue.tsx` composes `Card`, `Button`,
+  `Alert`, `StatusPill` and paperclip/file icons using the existing attachment
+  presentation. Its rows are **UI view models**, not attachment/API DTOs.
+  Queued rows may expose Remove; failed uploads may expose Retry; unknown
+  uploads may expose Check. Download and each applicable action appear only
+  when supplied. Busy disables operations. File selection forwards the actual
+  `File` objects; this component validates, stores and uploads nothing.
+- `components/supplier-invoice-creation-result.tsx` accepts a supplied unknown
+  or confirmed outcome. Unknown offers original-attempt checking without an
+  invoice ID or new-creation action. Confirmed requires the saved invoice ID,
+  actual selected Order label and explicit next action; an originating Order
+  label remains separate. Document presentation is supplied in both cases.
+- `localization/supplier-invoice-create-labels.ts` provides EN/EL built-in
+  presentation copy through the existing `LabelsProvider` / `useLocale`.
+
+`SupplierInvoiceCreateSlots` requires complete labelled field controls, with
+their error associations. The eventual controller must use `useAppForm` from
+`#/components/form` for the nontrivial integrated form. It owns the draft and
+file bytes **above** conditionally mounted tab panels; presentation components
+do not retain a draft, validate values, calculate invoice type/status or perform
+operations. Supplied field controls must support long Greek text, authorization
+and keyboard access. Supply read-only source/status fields and exact decimal
+text; never pass amounts through `Number()` or the current PO Float serializer.
+
+The controller must render the result **instead of** an actionable Create form
+after unknown or confirmed creation. Unknown document display must not offer
+uploads while the invoice owner is unresolved. Confirmed callbacks must retain
+the returned owner and stable file keys; successful files must not upload again,
+and unknown uploads must reconcile before retry. The supplied next action must
+protect pending local bytes before starting another invoice or returning to
+FRO-349's originating Order. These are integration responsibilities, not behavior
+implemented by a `ReactNode` slot.
+
+## Dependencies blocking integration
+
+Inspected baseline: production `main` at
+`3820e89e8caa341261e2d48bcb282d93e1bb1d03`.
+
+| Capability                                               | Missing or incompatible source                                                                                                                                                 | Required owner / follow-up                                                                                                                                       |
+| -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Create/read/attempt recovery and exact decimal transport | No Supplier Invoice entity or operations in the current database/GraphQL/REST references. Existing billing invoices are fixtures.                                              | FRO-321: delivered contracts, validation, duplicates, retry/concurrency and original-attempt reconciliation.                                                     |
+| Staff-only invoice access                                | `../auth/types.ts` contains no invoice authority. Participant PO access is insufficient.                                                                                       | FRO-321: authority and record/company scope, including source/reference access.                                                                                  |
+| Explicit regime/type eligibility                         | No explicit customs regime or Entry Note model at this baseline; existing PO Greece/ΚΤΑ/ΑΛΚ values cannot substitute.                                                          | FRO-356 / FRO-321: authoritative source and type computation.                                                                                                    |
+| Order search                                             | Backend `PurchaseOrderRepository.searchCondition` does not search Supplier/Client names. Existing list is paginated with a size cap of 100.                                    | Delivered authorized search must implement the approved semantics across pages. No first-100 local filtering.                                                    |
+| Currency and Client vessel sources                       | Countries supply currencies; `CompanyService.getCompany` supplies company vessels under COMPANY_VIEW.                                                                          | Confirm invoice-compatible reference access and complete authorized options.                                                                                     |
+| Invoice-owned documents                                  | `../attachments/types.ts` supports only PO/Shipment ownership; the existing panel immediately queries/uploads against a saved numeric owner and selects PO_EDIT/SHIPMENT_EDIT. | FRO-321: invoice ownership, authority, upload and reconciliation contracts. Do not reuse the persisted panel as a pre-create queue.                              |
+| Entry Note lookup                                        | No lookup at this baseline.                                                                                                                                                    | FRO-319 / FRO-321: later direct/inherited lookup. Basic capture must distinguish unavailable from confirmed absence without depending on that later integration. |
+
+The remaining frontend controller must implement source loading/error/denied
+states and stale-result handling, remote Order search, focusable unavailable-type
+reason, conditional confirmation, exact validation, dirty Cancel/new-draft guards,
+in-app draft/file lifetime and unload warning, submission and upload recovery,
+authority guards, selected-Order consumer refresh and actual navigation. No
+durable/reload-resilient storage is implied. These components must remain
+unconnected until the relevant contracts exist and are verified.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run from `frontline-forwarding-client/` with Node 22.13.0:
+
+```sh
+npm run test -- src/features/supplier-invoices --maxWorkers=2
+npm run test -- --maxWorkers=2
+npm run build
+npm run format:check
+npx prettier --check src/features/supplier-invoices
+npx tsc --noEmit
+```
+
+Tests exercise controlled exact-text and selected-file retention through tabs
+and locale changes, field order, local keyboard tab activation, applicable row
+callbacks, busy/action omission, and distinct unknown/confirmed result rendering.
+They do not establish server validation, permission or recovery correctness.
+Browser fixtures and screenshots are review evidence outside the delivered app;
+no fixture service or normal application route is included here.
+
+The unmodified baseline fails `npm ci` because `package.json` and
+`package-lock.json` differ. Verification uses a local-only
+`npm install --package-lock=false` without modifying either file; exact locked
+reproducibility remains unresolved. Baseline type checking reports two TS2352
+casts in `delivery-note-service.test.ts` (lines 77 and 81), and baseline formatting
+reports 270 files at the unchanged committed base. Keep those pre-existing findings separate from this feature's
+focused checks. No GraphQL documents changed, so codegen is not applicable.
+
+Design authority: [DESIGN.md](../../../DESIGN.md),
+[theme.css](../../styles/theme.css) and the current shared component source.
+The private Site is a design reference, not a runtime dependency.
